  "question": {
    "text": "Two concentric circular coils, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, are placed in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> plane. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn></math>turns, and a radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> has 200 turns and radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mtext>.</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> carries a time dependent current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in s. The emf induced in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mV</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> at the instant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>s is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is&nbsp;..........",
